  The output tensor's i'th dimension has `input.dims(i) * multiples[i]` elements,
  and the values of `input` are replicated `multiples[i]` times along the 'i'th
  dimension. For example, tiling `[a b c d]` by `[2]` produces
  `[a b c d a b c d]`.

